==Enemy==
Cadaver Bear has long range for a Zombie enemy, [[Burrow|burrows]] far past cats, gets knocked back only four times and, with its very fast attack cycle, it can push with terrifying ease, destroying many non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] units in up to two hits (especially when buffed). It even [[Revive|revives]] with 100% HP instead of the usual 50%.

==Strategy==
It's recommended to stall this enemy with tons of (preferably strong) meatshields. '''DO NOT USE ANY ATTACKERS WITH UNDER 360 RANGE''' (the only exceptions are [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] if you wish to exploit short-ranged peons as stepping stones), as its rapid attacks will tear them to pieces in no time flat. Therefore, the only [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] that can outrange this monster are [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] and [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] (365 and 390 respectively), with the Target [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] [[Talents|Talent]]. Although Corrupted Psychocat has been well-known to be a reliable support unit, he mostly fails to slow down Cadaver Bear due to his speed and short range differences. Cataur, however, can be a very potent attacker, especially with the [[Zombie Killer]] Talent unlocked. Tanky units such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] can also be used to chip or stall Cadaver Bear, hopefully down to a point where you could then send a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] to finish it off.

All units from the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] event are exceptional counters to this enemy, as long as they're protected by meatshields, as their range generally keeps them safe while their anti-zombie abilities could handle it well. As a rule of thumb, '''DO NOT LET CADAVER BEAR REVIVE UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES'''. Best case scenario, it revives at the enemy base, giving you a little bit more trouble. Worst case scenario, it revives in front of or in the middle of your attackers and quickly demolishes them. Its burrow could also prove problematic, so be prepared to have your [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] ready.

